From c0212731f6c04b3c94d1a9965e3d148d9cc11e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:05:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Smarter sample streaming: loading priority, more read-ahead,
 kit RAM saver

- storage/cluster/cluster_priority_queue: the loading queue sorts by
  priority, most urgent first and first come first served among equal
  priorities. 1.2.1 inserted each cluster by its address and then
  overwrote that sort key with the priority, so the loading order had
  nothing to do with urgency: a playing voice's next cluster could wait
  behind the starts of samples that may never play.
- A playing voice now holds three clusters from its play position on
  (kNumClustersReaderAhead) instead of two, so each load has two
  clusters' playing time to arrive instead of one. Sample starts stay
  pinned with two clusters.
- SampleHolderForVoice: short samples (up to four clusters) are held in
  RAM whole, as intended. 1.2.1 computed the byte for the rest as
  (start + clusterSizeMagnitude) << 1, inside the first cluster, so it
  held the first two clusters twice and the rest could be evicted.
- Kit RAM saver (community feature, on by default): once a second, kit
  rows without notes in any clip of the song let go of the pinned
  starts of their samples (usually 64 KB each), and rows that get notes
  claim them again. Kits with the kit arpeggiator on or with MIDI
  learned, and rows with MIDI learned, keep theirs.
- A voice whose sample start isn't in RAM yet (such a row, evicted)
  waits for it (up to 100 ms) and plays from the beginning, instead of
  dropping the hit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
