+#pragma once
+
+// Kit RAM saver (mastertune-v9, community feature, on by default).
+//
+// Every sample of a kit keeps the start of its audio (two clusters, usually 64 KB) pinned in RAM, so a hit plays at
+// once. For kit rows that have no notes in any clip of the song, that's RAM held for nothing: a kit of 50 samples of
+// which a song uses 5 pins about 3 MB. This lets go of the starts of those rows, so the RAM can serve as cache for
+// what's actually playing. The samples stay in the kit and their clusters stay cached until the RAM is needed for
+// something else. As soon as a row gets notes again, its start is claimed and loaded again.
+//
+// Rows that can sound without notes keep their starts: all rows of a kit with the kit arpeggiator on or with MIDI
+// learned for the whole kit, and rows with MIDI learned for themselves. Auditioning or playing a row whose start got
+// evicted waits for it to load (a few milliseconds) instead of dropping the hit, see VoiceUnisonPartSource::noteOn().
+namespace kit_ram_saver {
+
+// Main loop, about once a second
+void routine();
+
+} // namespace kit_ram_saver
